    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267-a8">

                <pb facs="0482" n="1442" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1442"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8 in No.
                    271.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de la Torre to
                        Mr. Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 6,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your attentive letter of the
                    5th instant, I have the honor to inform you that Spanish vessels arriving here
                    from Puerto Rico in ballast and sailing afterwards loaded with sugar for the
                    United States, pay tonnage dues at the rate of 25 cents for each 1,000 kilos
                    gross, excepting those Spanish steamers of periodical trips, which enjoy an
                    exemption from their payment.</p>
                <p>The tonnage dues collected in Puerto Rico do not serve as a basis at all in this
                    island, because of the different manner in which they are collected.</p>
                <p>God guard you many years.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alfonso de la
                    Torre.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
